## Summary

Adds read-only Stripe Connect reconciliation for payouts that are already `SUBMITTED`, so doFast can recover safely when a terminal Stripe webhook is delayed or missed.

## Safety invariants

- Reconciliation never creates a new Stripe Transfer or connected-account Payout.
- `SUBMITTED` payouts are never returned to the normal dispatch queue.
- Reconciliation does not increment payout dispatch `attempt_count`.
- Provider read failures, unknown statuses and identity mismatches keep the payout `SUBMITTED` and keep wallet funds reserved.
- Only `paid`, `failed` and `canceled` provider states enter the existing terminal settlement path.
- Failed/canceled Stripe payouts still reverse the original platform Transfer before `PAYOUT_RESTORE` can restore wallet funds.
- Existing source-of-funds restoration remains authoritative.
- Webhook/reconciliation races remain idempotent through the existing provider settlement boundary.

## Implementation

- adds a transactional `SUBMITTED` reconciliation queue with `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`;
- reuses `next_attempt_at` as a status-scoped reconciliation lease/backoff without a new migration;
- retrieves the existing Stripe connected-account Payout by stored `provider_reference`;
- validates payout id, amount, currency, doFast payout/user metadata, transfer reference and connected account;
- delegates terminal states to the existing Stripe Connect settlement service;
- adds an independent reconciliation scheduler/kill switch;
- allows reconciliation to remain enabled when live dispatch is disabled.

## Configuration

- `PAYOUT_SUBMITTED_RECONCILIATION_SECONDS` controls the initial grace period and provider-read lease/backoff;
- `PAYOUT_STRIPE_CONNECT_RECONCILIATION_ENABLED` independently enables read-only reconciliation;
- `PAYOUT_STRIPE_CONNECT_RECONCILIATION_INTERVAL_MS` controls scheduler cadence.

Production and local Compose forward all three settings. The production Compose contract verifies that forwarding. Sandbox payout CI keeps reconciliation explicitly disabled.

## Coverage

Focused tests cover:

- `PROCESSING -> SUBMITTED` reconciliation scheduling without another wallet mutation;
- due-row claim leasing without increasing dispatch attempts;
- provider failure/healthy bookkeeping while remaining `SUBMITTED`;
- read-only `pending`/`in_transit` handling;
- strict Stripe payout identity validation;
- terminal settlement delegation;
- scheduler fail-closed behavior;
- existing reversal-before-wallet-restore settlement remains covered.

The exact branch head `31acacd98e0b9dfd63f359acc963e3113351edfd` already passed push CI: API verify, Web verify, Production Compose contract and the full container/runtime smoke.

## Operational note

The ordinary sandbox smoke intentionally does not fabricate a Stripe connected-account Payout. A true Stripe test-mode Express-account E2E remains a separate P0 launch gate because only that can validate the actual external provider lifecycle end to end.

## Merge gate

Do not merge unless all PR-triggered workflows and push-triggered CI are green for the exact same latest head SHA. Merge method must be a merge commit.
